course: dictionary
lesson: 16041
title: Formal words and their feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to older books or to a formal voice, the careful way people speak in letters or speeches. «To her great vexation, the train was late.» The words around vexation give the clue: the train was late, and she was not pleased. So vexation must mean a feeling of being annoyed.
explain: Vexation can also mean the thing that causes the annoyance. «Losing his keys again was a constant vexation to Sam.» Here the keys are the problem, so vexation means something that annoys you. Ask yourself: is this a feeling, or the thing that causes it?
explain: In everyday talk, people usually say annoyance or frustration instead. If you read vexation in an old story, you can swap in one of those words and check that the sentence still makes sense. Vexed is an adjective meaning annoyed, and vexing means annoying.
fact: Vexation is a noun, and it is formal or old-fashioned.
fact: «Vexation» means a feeling of being annoyed, frustrated or worried.
fact: «Vexation» can also mean something that annoys you.
fact: In everyday speech, people say «annoyance» or «frustration» instead.
fact: «Vexed» is the adjective, meaning annoyed; «vexing» means annoying.
exercise: «To her great vexation, the train was late.» What does vexation mean here? | A big, happy party | *Annoyance and frustration | Feeling of being annoyed | A long, quiet walk
exercise: «Losing his keys again was a constant vexation to Sam.» What is the vexation in this sentence? | *Losing his keys again | Sam's new bike | A sunny morning | A party invitation
exercise: Which everyday word means much the same as vexation? | Sleepiness | Calmness | *Frustration | Delight
test: Which word is the adjective meaning annoyed? | *vexed | vexations | vexation
test: «Her ______ grew when the bus did not come.» Which word fits best? | breakfast | sunshine | lullaby | *vexation
exam: «He sighed with vexation when the printer jammed again.» What does vexation mean here? | Feeling very happy | Something made of paper | A quiet place to sit | *Feeling annoyed and frustrated
